1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,750
Every morning, planes drew white lines
across the sky over Addis. I used to

2
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:06,410
think they were writing to me.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:12,368
So I chased them. Documentaries at
midnight, not to study, just to be near

4
00:00:12,168 --> 00:00:15,010
it. Whatever I could find online, I
read.

5
00:00:15,810 --> 00:00:18,330
I watched landings the way other kids
watched football.

6
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:25,007
Then the national airline opened a
sponsored trainee pilot program. I

7
00:00:24,807 --> 00:00:25,470
applied.

8
00:00:26,810 --> 00:00:32,440
Age. Documents. Written test. Passed.
Interview. Passed.

9
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:38,564
In the simulator, my hands knew what to
do before I did. English proficiency.

10
00:00:38,364 --> 00:00:39,030
Passed.

11
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:44,310
One test left. The medical. My eyes.

12
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:48,890
Not cleared. Two words, and the sky
closed.

13
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:53,700
For weeks, I couldn't look up.

14
00:00:56,240 --> 00:01:01,309
But the sky never asked for my eyes. It
asked for my curiosity. So I kept

15
00:01:01,109 --> 00:01:03,110
learning, and I built this.

16
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:09,994
My eyes failed one test. My curiosity
hasn't failed one yet. I'm not done

17
00:01:09,794 --> 00:01:10,680
looking up.
